# Skill Runtime（locked）

Full spec: `docs/SKILL_RUNTIME.md`

**Doctrine:** UI belongs to components; business logic belongs to optional Skills. Components never know that Skill Runtime exists.

## Package boundary

- Source: `packages/skill/`.
- Public subpaths: `amg-webui/skill/core` (framework-free) and `amg-webui/skill` (Core + Vue integration).
- Internal alias: `@amg-webui/skill`.
- Root `amg-webui` entry **must not** re-export Skill APIs.
- `skill/core` must not import Vue, components, theme, locale, telemetry, browser globals, or a backend client.
- `packages/components/**` must not import Skill or add Skill-only props.
- “Zero cost when unused” means no runtime bundle dependency when the subpath is not imported; do not claim zero install size.

## SR1 / SR2 scope

This delivery contains:

- `defineSkill` · `createSkillRuntime` · `createSkillPipeline` · `createSkillPipelineExecutor`
- `createSkillPlugin` · `vSkill` · `AmgSkillScope`
- Unit / Context / Runtime / Scope
- Pipeline sequence (top-level `items`) / parallel / if / retry / fallback
- registered Condition, Adapter, Observer

Official built-ins, Telemetry bridge, DevTools, debug UI and low-code editor are SR3 / SR4 follow-ups. Do not invent imports or mark them shipped.

## Isolation and lifecycle

- Every mount/run gets a unique `instanceId`, private `ctx.state`, AbortController and context-managed resources.
- Scope owns its event bus, explicit `scope.state` and mounted handles; Unit / Adapter / Observer remain Runtime-owned and Conditions remain Executor-owned.
- Unit definitions stay stateless; never store per-instance data in module globals.
- `ctx.on()` returns an unsubscribe function. Runtime cleans remaining listeners on dispose.
- `dispose()` and teardown are idempotent. Late async setup results cannot reactivate a disposed instance.
- Setup failure, cancellation, Scope disposal and Vue unmount all enter the same cleanup path.
- Do not reuse the global `EventService` as the internal Skill context bus.

## Types

- Public APIs use generics / `unknown`; no `any`, bare `Function`, unsafe public casts or untyped event handlers.
- Normalize unknown failures into the `SkillRuntimeError` / `SkillExecutionError` / `SkillAbortError` family while preserving execution context and cause.
- Abort is control flow, not a retryable ordinary error.
- Host access uses an explicit, minimal public capability object; never inspect Vue private proxies or internal reactive state.

## Pipeline safety

- Definition version: `{ version: 1, items: [...] }`.
- Top-level `items` are the sequence; nodes are `skill | parallel | if | retry | fallback`.
- Pipeline JSON contains JSON values only: no functions, DOM/Vue instances, Symbols, cycles or dynamic imports.
- `if.condition` resolves only a trusted predicate registered through `executor.registerCondition(name, fn)`.
- **Never** use `eval`, `new Function`, arbitrary expression strings or template-code evaluation.
- Unknown predicates / skills / adapters fail fast with structured errors.
- `retry.max` is the total attempt count and must be an integer from 1 to 10. Retry handles `SkillExecutionError` by default and skips abort / registry / config errors; external side effects require idempotency.
- Fallback handles `SkillExecutionError` only; it must not mask abort, unknown registration or configuration failures.
- Parallel failure still cancels or awaits sibling cleanup.

## Adapter and Observer

- Adapters receive `SkillContext` (including its `AbortSignal`) and own backend DTO mapping; Skills do not bind to response envelopes.
- Core has no implicit network, auth, console or cloud reporting.
- Observer failures never alter Skill/Pipeline results.
- Observer events omit raw config/payload by default; never leak auth tokens or sensitive data.
- Default Console Observer and directive reporting omit raw Error details; full errors require an explicit application-owned handler or opt-in.
- Telemetry stays default-off and may integrate later through an external Observer bridge; Core does not import telemetry.

## Vue integration

- `AmgSkillScope` only provides/injects Scope and handles lifecycle; it does not render business UI.
- `createSkillPlugin({ runtime })` registers `v-skill` / `AmgSkillScope` against an explicit Runtime; it must not create a hidden global Runtime.
- `vSkill` mounts on `mounted`, rebinds after binding reference change, disposes old before new, and always disposes on `unmounted`; callers replace binding objects instead of mutating config in place.
- Composition code obtains Scope with `useSkillScope()`; directive bindings pass `scope` explicitly instead of inspecting Vue private component internals.
- Directive bindings pass an explicit versioned `host` capability when needed; DOM / Vue instances are never implicit hosts.
- SSR import is side-effect free; DOM work starts only in client lifecycle hooks.
- Removing `v-skill` must leave the component's existing Props / Emits / Slots / Expose behavior unchanged.

## Verification before “done”

- Run at least `npx vue-tsc --noEmit`, Skill unit tests and `npm run build:lib`.
- Test registration conflicts, multi-instance isolation, nested Scope, cancellation races, idempotent teardown, Adapter abort, Observer failure isolation, every Pipeline node, forbidden/unknown predicates, Vue rebind/unmount, SSR core import and package exports.
- Verify `amg-webui/skill/core` works without Vue/DOM, `amg-webui/skill` exposes Vue integration, and root `amg-webui` does not expose Skill APIs.
- Do not turn roadmap language such as “100%”, “zero cost”, “full coverage” into a completion claim without measured evidence.
